// The `raw` field of an object (flush.id): the function itself for a plain
// function used as a value, which is what a native's function-pointer
// parameter is given, and 0 for the template of a bind, because no function
// pointer is a closure. clo_fixture and clo_seeded are what the cases of the
// closure emitters share: fx_target(int x) return int, registered with the
// C type column, and with fx_target noted as a plain value.

fv_raw(string name, int nd) {
  string s = "0";
  if(nd == 0) {
    s = "(void*)" + fn_sym(name);
  }
} return string s;
given clo_fixture ("tick", 0):("(void*)id_tick")
("tick", 3):("0")

